                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This was probably the longest HOG/Adventure I've ever played, dozens of locations, incredible amount of value. The story was pretty original and really worked. There were lots of characters, including real ones like FMV but only in cut scenes. The perfect amount of dialog. You almost always knew what to do next and which objects to use. The only complaint is i didn't like the dominos matching puzzles but that's just me and towards the middle to the end, the HOPs became more frequent and more cluttered. But that's me just bitching since they also offered a ton of value. There were zillions of great sounds and all of the scenes, objects and menus were very nicely detailed and polished. This was one of the best Adventure/HOGs I've every played in forever. Oh and the secret bonus bonus feature when you finish is pretty cool and funny. Very cozy game, perfect to cuddle up with a nice soup or coffee or both!",
